1
00:00:00,196 --> 00:00:00,836
哈喽大家好
Hi everyone

2
00:00:01,326 --> 00:00:04,896
本期我们一起来学习一下价格歧视这个名词
This episode we're learning a term: price discrimination

3
00:00:05,475 --> 00:00:08,385
价格歧视这个名词一句话的定义呢是
The one-line definition of price discrimination is

4
00:00:08,770 --> 00:00:12,650
同一个商品或服务对于不同的人的数量
the same product or service, sold to different people, in different quantities

5
00:00:13,029 --> 00:00:16,119
或者不同的场合去收取不同的价格
or on different occasions, at different prices

6
00:00:16,475 --> 00:00:19,795
而价格的差异并不是因为它们的成本不同
and the price gap isn't because their costs differ

7
00:00:20,168 --> 00:00:21,978
这里有两个关键的节点
There are two key points here

8
00:00:22,379 --> 00:00:24,849
第一 卖的是同一种东西
First, it's the same thing being sold

9
00:00:25,189 --> 00:00:27,199
或者是本质上相同的一样东西
or essentially the same thing

10
00:00:27,999 --> 00:00:31,161
第二是 价差不能用成本去解释
Second, the price gap can't be explained by cost

11
00:00:31,486 --> 00:00:34,456
不是因为成本升值而导致价格差异
It's not that costs went up and so the price changed

12
00:00:35,196 --> 00:00:36,310
这里是像素呼吸的
This is Pixel Breath's

13
00:00:36,310 --> 00:00:38,646
100个经济学原理第11个
100 Principles of Economics, number 11

14
00:00:39,246 --> 00:00:40,066
价格歧视
Price discrimination

15
00:00:41,290 --> 00:00:44,360
价格歧视呢 其实有三种不同的形式
Price discrimination actually comes in three forms

16
00:00:44,716 --> 00:00:45,849
这种三级的分法呢
This three-degree classification

17
00:00:45,950 --> 00:00:50,346
是庇古在1920年福利经济学里提出来的
was proposed by Pigou in The Economics of Welfare in 1920

18
00:00:50,696 --> 00:00:51,431
讲了一百多年
It's been taught for over a hundred years

19
00:00:51,496 --> 00:00:54,926
教科书依旧在用这个非常经典的分法
and textbooks still use this classic framework

20
00:00:55,325 --> 00:00:57,685
它有用的原因不是因为传统
It's useful not because of tradition

21
00:00:58,245 --> 00:01:02,035
而是它切中的是价格歧视中最核心的那个问题
but because it hits the core question of price discrimination

22
00:01:02,661 --> 00:01:05,111
商家为什么知道该收谁的钱
how does a seller know whom to charge more?

23
00:01:05,467 --> 00:01:09,007
价格歧视的关键难点不是我想多收钱
The hard part isn't wanting to charge more

24
00:01:09,409 --> 00:01:12,659
而是我怎么知道用户心里的那个价格呢
it's how do I know the price in the customer's head?

25
00:01:13,011 --> 00:01:16,231
这三级正好对应三种不同的信息来源
The three degrees match three different sources of information

26
00:01:16,951 --> 00:01:17,881
首先第一级是
The first degree is

27
00:01:18,233 --> 00:01:19,783
商家认识你这个人
the seller knows you personally

28
00:01:20,203 --> 00:01:22,003
知道你最多愿意出多少
knows the most you're willing to pay

29
00:01:22,623 --> 00:01:24,623
所以会按照人头去定价
so it sets a price per head

30
00:01:24,993 --> 00:01:29,933
对每个顾客去收取他愿意付的最高价
charging each customer the highest price they'd pay

31
00:01:30,306 --> 00:01:31,976
比如 菜市场的砍价
For example, haggling at the market

32
00:01:32,328 --> 00:01:35,059
或者拍卖 再或者大数据杀熟
or auctions, or big-data price gouging

33
00:01:35,394 --> 00:01:39,267
这都是卖家期望用买家心里的最高价
In all of these, the seller hopes to close the deal

34
00:01:39,479 --> 00:01:40,759
去进行一次交易
at the top price in the buyer's mind

35
00:01:41,131 --> 00:01:43,111
第二级是 商家不认识你
The second degree: the seller doesn't know you

36
00:01:43,411 --> 00:01:44,941
所以只好摆出几个版本
so it has to lay out several versions

37
00:01:45,231 --> 00:01:47,281
去让你暴露自己的意图
to make you reveal your intent

38
00:01:47,635 --> 00:01:49,215
比如 第二件半价
For example, second item half price

39
00:01:49,755 --> 00:01:53,074
再比如 软件会区分为专业版和普通版
or software split into Pro and Standard editions

40
00:01:53,422 --> 00:01:55,772
同一架飞机上区分了经济舱
or the same plane divided into economy

41
00:01:56,012 --> 00:01:57,282
商务舱和头等舱
business and first class

42
00:01:57,642 --> 00:02:00,142
其实 本质上都是一种价格歧视
At heart, these are all price discrimination

43
00:02:00,504 --> 00:02:01,894
最后一级是按照
The last degree sorts people

44
00:02:02,260 --> 00:02:05,280
可识别的群体特征进行一次区分
by identifiable group characteristics

45
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:08,401
比如同一个景区分为学生票
For example, the same scenic spot has student tickets

46
00:02:08,971 --> 00:02:10,360
成人票和老年票
adult tickets and senior tickets

47
00:02:10,694 --> 00:02:12,400
而不同的地方性景区
and some local attractions

48
00:02:12,611 --> 00:02:14,802
还会存在本地人门票优惠
also offer discounts to residents

49
00:02:15,015 --> 00:02:17,839
当然它们都是针对于不同的人群
All of these target different groups

50
00:02:17,839 --> 00:02:20,335
去进行不同的价格收取
and charge them different prices

51
00:02:20,867 --> 00:02:22,367
这个因素会有很多
There are many factors behind this

52
00:02:22,617 --> 00:02:24,437
比如会有国家的支持等等
such as government support

53
00:02:24,764 --> 00:02:26,359
当然 以上三种方式
Of course, all three

54
00:02:26,359 --> 00:02:30,224
其实都是价格歧视的不同体现
are different forms of price discrimination

55
00:02:31,425 --> 00:02:33,745
那么这里我们要想的其实就是
So what we need to ask here is

56
00:02:34,185 --> 00:02:36,015
为什么商家可以这样做呢
why can sellers do this?

57
00:02:36,675 --> 00:02:39,995
其实 有三点决定了商家拥有这样的权利
Three things give sellers this power

58
00:02:40,362 --> 00:02:41,606
第一是 它有定价权
First, pricing power

59
00:02:41,606 --> 00:02:44,852
这部分不是所有的竞争市场都可以做的
Not every competitive market allows this

60
00:02:45,195 --> 00:02:47,331
只有垄断或者一些强势的商家
Only monopolies or some strong sellers

61
00:02:47,331 --> 00:02:50,425
才可以进行一些定价权上的操作
can play with pricing like that

62
00:02:50,781 --> 00:02:54,351
第二 它可以区分顾客谁愿意多付一些价钱
Second, it can tell which customers will pay more

63
00:02:54,771 --> 00:02:56,777
比如学生证 比如大数据杀熟
through a student ID, through big data

64
00:02:56,854 --> 00:02:58,321
比如消费记录
through purchase history

65
00:02:58,671 --> 00:03:00,391
第三是防止转卖
Third, it prevents resale

66
00:03:00,743 --> 00:03:03,973
低价买到的人没有办法再进行高价的倒卖
Whoever bought cheap can't resell at a higher price

67
00:03:04,393 --> 00:03:05,783
所以电影票可以歧视
So movie tickets can be price-discriminated

68
00:03:06,033 --> 00:03:07,493
但是大米却不能歧视
but rice can't

69
00:03:08,123 --> 00:03:10,240
因为大米大家的价格都是透明的
because everyone knows the price of rice

70
00:03:10,317 --> 00:03:13,073
即使再低也不会低到哪去
and even the cheapest won't be much cheaper

71
00:03:13,436 --> 00:03:17,116
但是电影票就有不同的渠道以及不同的折扣
But movie tickets have different channels and different discounts

72
00:03:17,506 --> 00:03:18,616
叠加在一起之后
and once you stack them

73
00:03:18,926 --> 00:03:20,956
有可能会买到一个非常低的价格
you might get a very low price

74
00:03:21,492 --> 00:03:23,742
像上上周我们一起去看的生化危机
Like Resident Evil, which we saw together two weeks ago

75
00:03:23,742 --> 00:03:26,892
就以30多的价格拿到了70块钱的电影票
I got a 70-yuan ticket for just 30-something

76
00:03:27,312 --> 00:03:30,082
这就是一个非常典型的价格歧视
That's a textbook case of price discrimination

77
00:03:31,306 --> 00:03:34,296
接下来我们会举一些简单的生活中的例子
Next, let's look at some simple everyday examples

78
00:03:34,659 --> 00:03:36,409
去一起看一下价格歧视
of price discrimination

79
00:03:36,762 --> 00:03:38,300
最简单的莫不过于
The simplest one is

80
00:03:38,300 --> 00:03:41,911
安卓手机打车和iOS手机打车
ride-hailing on an Android phone versus on an iPhone

81
00:03:41,911 --> 00:03:43,712
在定价上是不一样的
the pricing isn't the same

82
00:03:44,312 --> 00:03:46,042
这叫做大数据杀熟
This is called big-data price gouging

83
00:03:46,612 --> 00:03:47,935
App会根据你的消费
The app looks at your spending

84
00:03:47,935 --> 00:03:51,502
给新老用户或者给苹果用户更高的价格
and quotes new or old users, or iPhone users, a higher price

85
00:03:51,876 --> 00:03:54,266
这是数字时代的一级价格歧视
This is first-degree price discrimination in the digital age

86
00:03:54,644 --> 00:03:57,644
同一个软件按照不同的版本进行定价
The same software priced by edition

87
00:03:57,904 --> 00:03:59,144
比如它们功能都一样
the features are all the same

88
00:03:59,394 --> 00:04:00,514
但砍掉几个按钮
but cut a few buttons

89
00:04:00,814 --> 00:04:02,004
价格就会便宜一半
and the price drops by half

90
00:04:02,394 --> 00:04:04,314
这其实是二级歧视
That's second-degree discrimination

91
00:04:04,693 --> 00:04:06,774
同一个景区 本地人半价
The same scenic spot, half price for locals

92
00:04:06,832 --> 00:04:08,913
而用身份证去区分不同的群体
using ID cards to separate the groups

93
00:04:09,253 --> 00:04:11,663
这其实是三级价格歧视
That's third-degree price discrimination

94
00:04:12,027 --> 00:04:16,117
本期带大家一起去见识了价格歧视这个名词
This episode introduced you to the term price discrimination

95
00:04:16,486 --> 00:04:17,926
那么我们下期再见
See you next time

